# ============================================================================
# Deterministic byte representation — this file is a PROVENANCE control, not a
# style preference.
#
# spec_sha256 (docs/FrozenB0_MasterPreregistration.md) and every entry in
# NORMATIVE_MODULES are RAW-BYTE identities. A checkout whose line endings
# depend on the platform, on core.autocrlf, or on whoever cloned the repo would
# produce a different hash for identical content, and the seal would bind
# nothing. LF is the canonical repository representation: HEAD has stored these
# paths as LF throughout, so this file records the existing convention rather
# than migrating it.
#
# Established 2026-08-18 during Repo & Provenance Finalization Closure.
# Before this file existed, .gitattributes was ABSENT and 150 tracked files had
# drifted to CRLF in the working tree (content-identical). They were restored to
# their HEAD bytes rather than committed, because 3 of them are Frozen A
# protected files, which must not be modified.
# ============================================================================

# Default: normalize to LF in the repository AND in the working tree.
* text=auto eol=lf

# --- Binary: never line-ending converted, never diffed as text ---------------
# These carry incidental \r\n byte pairs that are DATA, not line terminators.
# 122 tracked .parquet, 1 .npz and 1 .docx were verified to contain such pairs;
# relying on the text=auto heuristic alone would risk corrupting them.
*.parquet  -text
*.npz      -text
*.xlsx     -text
*.xls      -text
*.docx     -text
*.zip      -text
*.png      -text
*.jpg      -text
*.pdf      -text
*.pyc      -text

# --- Windows script hosts require CRLF at execution time ---------------------
# Still deterministic: the repository stores LF, and the working-tree ending is
# fixed by this file rather than by platform configuration.
*.bat  text eol=crlf
*.cmd  text eol=crlf
*.ps1  text eol=crlf
*.vbs  text eol=crlf
